# L §5.18 example ask q7, copied; Partial answers: "A line marked partial prints, when its value is a hole, its
# known part and the named holes it is linear in, each with its coefficient ... (412 300.00 PLN + 1 × ?"value of
# the firm share")."  flat + savings = 400 000.00 + 12 300.00 = 412 300.00 PLN; the firm share is a hole row.
# Without partial the line is the plain hole.  "A rounding ... meeting a hole makes the line a plain hole".
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input flat: money PLN
input savings: money PLN
input firm_share: money PLN

def estate_value: money PLN at reader
  rule base = flat + savings + firm_share
def rounded: money PLN at reader
  rule base = round(estate_value, 1 PLN, half-up)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  flat = 400 000.00 PLN
  savings = 12 300.00 PLN
  firm_share = ?"value of the firm share"

ask q7: estate_value law 2026-06-30 partial
ask q7b: estate_value law 2026-06-30
ask q7c: rounded law 2026-06-30 partial
=== expect
q7: 412 300.00 PLN + 1 × ?"value of the firm share" (firm_share)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q7b: ?"value of the firm share" (firm_share)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q7c: ?"value of the firm share" (firm_share)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
